// expect: refuse P_UnexpectedToken
// A `]` stands where the second arm's pattern belongs. The parser recovers so
// it can keep judging the rest of the module, and the pattern it recovers to
// is a guess at text it could not read, so the program refuses. Until
// 2026-10-16 a parse error was a warning: the guess was a wildcard, and on
// boot 969f2559 `pick(7)` answered 20, the arm after it never reached.
fn pick(n) = match n {
  0 => 10,
  ] => 20,
  _ => 30,
}

fn main() = pick(7)
